WEBVTT

00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:17.516
Who knew repairing
the station grid

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.040
would involve
so much sprinting?

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:21.129
No talk. Sleep.

00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:25.002
-What the? Hey, no, no. Down.
-TENDI: I did it!

00:00:25.046 --> 00:00:26.960
-I updated the dog!
-Down.

00:00:27.004 --> 00:00:28.614
-What does that even mean?
Hey! Mm-mm.
-In Medical,

00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:30.094
-they encourage us
to do side projects.

00:00:30.138 --> 00:00:31.835
-No! Why?!
-So I took a bunch
of inert carbon

00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:33.750
-and built myself
a fluffy friend from scratch.
-Shut up!

00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:35.230
-No! Aah!
-It's supposed
to look like a dog.

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:37.101
-You know, from Earth.
- Tendi,

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:38.450
-please get it out of here.
-Oh, of course.

00:00:38.494 --> 00:00:40.322
Come here! Come here.

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:42.193
-Ah.
She's five percent faster

00:00:42.237 --> 00:00:44.108
and six percent smarter.
You know, I hand-edited

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:46.023
-all six billion sequences.
It was really fun!

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.112
-When did you even find time
for that?

00:00:48.156 --> 00:00:49.374
-Sometimes when I saythat I'm going to the bathroom,

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:51.376
I'm really recoding her DNA.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.161
This little lady's protein bondstotally accepted

00:00:53.204 --> 00:00:55.989
the Cas9 snipping without
any cellular degradation.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.253
Who has malleable protein bonds?You do.

00:00:58.296 --> 00:00:59.819
-Yes, you do.
-I don't get it.

00:00:59.863 --> 00:01:02.605
You could've built any life-format all, and you did this?

00:01:02.648 --> 00:01:03.997
It just looks like a normal dog.

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:06.261
That's exactly what
I was going for!

00:01:06.304 --> 00:01:08.132
I'll go grab my notes soI can read you the juicy parts.

00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:10.003
You're going to love howI reorganized her mitochondria.

00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:11.875
No spoilers, but...

00:01:11.918 --> 00:01:13.181
...it's super funny!

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:15.748
Just to be clear,
this is a normal dog,

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:16.967
and she's messing with us.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.152
-Oh, God. Not a normal dog.

00:01:28.196 --> 00:01:31.286
Wake me up if it turns intosomething I need to care about.

00:02:42.487 --> 00:02:45.011
RANSOM:
First officer's log. An elite team from the
Cerritos

00:02:45.055 --> 00:02:47.449
has been selected
by Admiral Syltrack to liaise

00:02:47.492 --> 00:02:50.408
with the Pisepian agricultural colony in disputed territory.

00:02:50.452 --> 00:02:52.236
Captain Freeman, Shaxs,
and myself

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.803
have been enlisted
to join the mission

00:02:53.846 --> 00:02:56.806
due to our expertise in the germination of rulot seeds.

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:58.851
In our absence,
theCerritos will receive

00:02:58.895 --> 00:03:02.072
a temporary transfer of command to a visiting captain.

00:03:04.335 --> 00:03:07.251
Visiting captain?
No! So lame.

00:03:07.295 --> 00:03:09.210
I figured you'd love a break
from our usual guys.

00:03:09.253 --> 00:03:11.255
Sub caps never know
what they're doing.

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:12.909
They're all like,
"Buffer the phase coils."

00:03:12.952 --> 00:03:14.737
And we're like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.999
What areyou talking about?

00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:17.261
I don't want
some babysitter Jellico-type

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:18.393
hovering over us

00:03:18.436 --> 00:03:19.959
when we're already going
to a bog planet,

00:03:20.003 --> 00:03:21.222
which is, like,
the worst kind of planets,

00:03:21.265 --> 00:03:22.484
as far as planets go.

00:03:22.527 --> 00:03:24.442
Bogs are actually fascinating.
Did you know

00:03:24.486 --> 00:03:25.748
-that the spore count can...
-I don't want to know
about a bog!

00:03:25.791 --> 00:03:27.097
It's a gross word
for a gross place!

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.186
Well, you're being
very unscientific.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.366
Anyway, I'm into it.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.194
We get to rub shoulders
with the visiting crew,

00:03:37.238 --> 00:03:39.065
maybe impress another captain.

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:41.329
Oh, you're just excited to kiss
a whole new butt, aren't you?

00:03:41.372 --> 00:03:42.634
Well, I wouldn't put it
like that.

00:03:42.678 --> 00:03:44.201
But yes, very.

00:03:45.202 --> 00:03:46.812
Hmm...

00:03:46.856 --> 00:03:48.205
-Rutherford!

00:03:48.249 --> 00:03:49.511
The visiting crew's
gonna be here any minute.

00:03:49.554 --> 00:03:51.295
Hey, if I part my hair
like this, do I look

00:03:51.339 --> 00:03:52.949
more promotable or less?

00:03:52.992 --> 00:03:54.472
More? Less?
More? Less?

00:03:54.516 --> 00:03:56.300
-Yeah, sure.
-You didn't even look!

00:03:56.344 --> 00:03:58.215
Sorry.
It's this transporter, man.

00:03:58.259 --> 00:04:00.696
I'm trying to make it go
.07 seconds faster.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.306
Mariner wouldn't help me
test it.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.308
She said she wanted to wait
until I ironed out the kinks.

00:04:04.352 --> 00:04:06.092
But how am I supposed to do thatif nobody's gonna

00:04:06.136 --> 00:04:07.877
-help me test it?
-Ooh! I'll do it.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.357
I can tell the new captain that,in my spare time,

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.184
-I enjoy improving efficiency.
-Okay, cool.

00:04:11.228 --> 00:04:12.403
I'll just transport you
back and forth

00:04:12.447 --> 00:04:14.318
super quick.
Real easy.

00:04:14.362 --> 00:04:15.493
Okay. Beam me up.
: I mean,

00:04:15.537 --> 00:04:17.539
Boim me up.
You know what I'm saying.

00:04:17.582 --> 00:04:20.455
-Okeydokey!

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.154
That was, like, half a second
faster than normal!

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.851
I can't believe it's working.

00:04:25.895 --> 00:04:26.896
Ooh, ooh, ooh!
Run me through it again!

00:04:26.939 --> 00:04:27.897
Do it again! Do it again!

00:04:32.945 --> 00:04:34.033
-Uh...
-Aw, man.

00:04:34.077 --> 00:04:35.644
-I thought I solved this.
-What?!

00:04:35.687 --> 00:04:37.950
Sorry, it's just the last part
of the transporter process!

00:04:37.994 --> 00:04:38.951
It can be a bit sticky!

00:04:38.995 --> 00:04:40.910
Sticky?! Am I gonna die?!

00:04:40.953 --> 00:04:43.086
No, no! You're just off by,
like, one millicochrane!

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:45.871
-It's just cosmetic!
-What's that noise?!

00:04:45.915 --> 00:04:46.872
Is that me?!

00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:48.309
You hardly notice it!

00:04:48.352 --> 00:04:50.311
You got to fix me before
the visiting crew gets here!

00:04:50.354 --> 00:04:52.356
-I can't look like this!
-What?!

00:04:58.275 --> 00:05:00.495
Oh, well, here we go.
Babysitter time

00:05:00.538 --> 00:05:02.758
in three, two, one...

00:05:04.716 --> 00:05:06.370
Amina?

00:05:06.414 --> 00:05:09.199
There she is!

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.635
Are you surprised?

00:05:10.679 --> 00:05:12.376
Oh, my gosh. I thought
you were on the Oakland.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:14.552
Eh, couldn't pass up
a water filtration repair.

00:05:14.596 --> 00:05:15.988
This is crazy!

00:05:16.032 --> 00:05:17.860
Wait, andyou're
a freakin' captain now?

00:05:17.903 --> 00:05:19.209
Get those title bumps, girl.

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.080
Yeah, I'm kind of a big deal.

00:05:21.124 --> 00:05:22.255
I've even got a team.

00:05:22.299 --> 00:05:23.605
Warren, Prachett, Durga,

00:05:23.648 --> 00:05:25.998
this is my old friend
I was telling you about.

00:05:26.042 --> 00:05:29.001
Captain Ramsey... speaks fondlyof your time at the Academy.

00:05:29.045 --> 00:05:30.655
Oh, boy.
What'd she tell you?

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:32.657
That when it comes
to boots-on-the-ground

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.572
planetary action,
you're the best.

00:05:34.616 --> 00:05:36.400
And you look damn good doing it.

00:05:36.444 --> 00:05:39.577
Curious
that you're still an ensign.

00:05:39.621 --> 00:05:40.883
-Ensign Boimler

00:05:40.926 --> 00:05:42.406
reporting for duty!

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:47.455
Dude! What is wrong with you?!

00:05:47.498 --> 00:05:49.413
Nothing! I'm just phasing!

00:05:49.457 --> 00:05:50.458
No biggie!

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:51.850
Disagree!
It's kind of a biggie!

00:05:51.894 --> 00:05:53.765
Ensign, report to sickbay!

00:05:53.809 --> 00:05:54.984
But that's for sick people!

00:05:55.027 --> 00:05:56.638
-Now!
-Aw.

00:06:00.032 --> 00:06:02.208
-How long is this going to last?!

00:06:02.252 --> 00:06:03.993
How am I supposed to know?!

00:06:04.036 --> 00:06:05.995
You looklike a goddamn science project!

00:06:06.038 --> 00:06:08.084
Then-- ow!-- why are you
still taking samples?!

00:06:08.127 --> 00:06:09.433
I figured it out!

00:06:11.348 --> 00:06:13.698
All right.
Boimler's back, baby!

00:06:13.742 --> 00:06:15.787
Time to kiss some visiting butt.

00:06:15.831 --> 00:06:17.136
Wait, I'm still all phase-y.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.225
Yeah. But you're
not making the sound anymore,

00:06:19.269 --> 00:06:20.444
which was the worst part,
right?

00:06:20.488 --> 00:06:21.706
Oh, yeah. That was terrible.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.229
-I'm literally hard to look at.-

00:06:23.273 --> 00:06:24.492
I mean, what if-- what if...

00:06:24.535 --> 00:06:27.016
Nobody wants a sparkly cap'n!

00:06:27.059 --> 00:06:28.583
Oh, all right, all right.
Calm down.

00:06:28.626 --> 00:06:30.323
-I already alerted Division 14.-

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:31.716
The time travel police?

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:34.415
No! D-14 handles
unsolvable space illnesses

00:06:34.458 --> 00:06:35.590
and science mysteries.

00:06:35.633 --> 00:06:37.287
And they can make me
a real boy again?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.203
They've got this great
medical spa on Endicronimas V.

00:06:40.246 --> 00:06:41.596
En...
Endicron...

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:43.032
Everyone just calls it
"The Farm."

00:06:43.075 --> 00:06:45.426
You'll be pampered and tended tolike a precious gem.

00:06:45.469 --> 00:06:48.472
You and Mr. Whatever The Hell
That Thing Is over there.

00:06:48.516 --> 00:06:50.213
Don't worry, The Dog.
I won't let them hurt you.

00:06:50.256 --> 00:06:51.736
Wait, you named it "The Dog"?

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.172
Of course. Why wouldn't I?

00:06:53.216 --> 00:06:54.565
She's a totally normal dog.

00:06:54.609 --> 00:06:56.611
Mm, I'm starting to think
you know more about DNA

00:06:56.654 --> 00:06:58.961
-than you do about dogs.
-We don't have any on Orion.

00:06:59.004 --> 00:07:00.441
-We're really missing out.
Dogs are great.

00:07:02.181 --> 00:07:04.401
-Aw, look at you.

00:07:04.445 --> 00:07:06.142
You're just
a cute little cinnamon roll.

00:07:06.185 --> 00:07:07.491
Yes, you are!

00:07:07.535 --> 00:07:08.797
Visiting captain's log.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:11.495
Stardate 57752.6.

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:14.367
The Cerritosis en route
to the planet Khwopa to...

00:07:14.411 --> 00:07:17.501
perform a repair of
their water filtration system.

00:07:17.545 --> 00:07:19.851
Once completed, we will...
 rendezvous

00:07:19.895 --> 00:07:21.505
-with the USS Rubidoux.End log.

00:07:21.549 --> 00:07:22.898
Will you stop it?

00:07:22.941 --> 00:07:25.291
Sorry, I just love
captains' trinkets, you know?

00:07:25.335 --> 00:07:27.511
Come on.
Give me the dirt.

00:07:27.555 --> 00:07:29.948
Have you seen
Ransom's photon torpedo?

00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:31.515
Barf! No! Disgusting.

00:07:31.559 --> 00:07:33.125
-No, for real, that is big barf.-

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:35.127
So, how long do we have you?

00:07:35.171 --> 00:07:36.520
I mean, it's gonna take a whileto catch you up

00:07:36.564 --> 00:07:37.869
on all the crazy stuff
I've been up to.

00:07:37.913 --> 00:07:40.393
Yeah. That's why I want you
at my side.

00:07:40.437 --> 00:07:42.395
Getting your perspective
on the Cerritoscrew

00:07:42.439 --> 00:07:43.875
would be invaluable.

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:46.574
I mean, come on, nobody likes
a babysitter captain.

00:07:46.617 --> 00:07:49.402
Babysitter captain? What?I don't even know what that is.

00:07:49.446 --> 00:07:51.535
-What?
-So, what do you say?

00:07:51.579 --> 00:07:53.406
Want to be my first officer?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.539
Oh! Of course!
You've got the dream team.

00:07:55.583 --> 00:07:57.410
It's about timethis bridge had a kickass crew.

00:07:57.454 --> 00:07:59.325
I mean, the usual guys are fine,
but they're kind of... eh.

00:07:59.369 --> 00:08:00.544
Oh, wait, are--
Wait, are you kidding?

00:08:00.588 --> 00:08:01.502
-No, you're kidding, right?

00:08:01.545 --> 00:08:03.416
-I'm not kidding!
-Then yes!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.506
All right. Let's do this...

00:08:05.549 --> 00:08:06.637
Number One.

00:08:31.619 --> 00:08:33.229
Greetings.

00:08:33.272 --> 00:08:36.667
I am the Division 14
medical specialist.

00:08:36.711 --> 00:08:39.670
Aw, thank you. I'm Tendi,
and this is my dog, The Dog.

00:08:39.714 --> 00:08:41.977
And let the record show
we're here under protest.

00:08:43.587 --> 00:08:44.719
I must warn you,

00:08:44.762 --> 00:08:47.504
stepping aboard this vessel
is consent

00:08:47.548 --> 00:08:49.854
to be surrounded
by dark abnormalities

00:08:49.898 --> 00:08:52.509
and the clinically obscene.

00:08:52.553 --> 00:08:54.555
Uh, how long will it take
to get to the spa?

00:08:54.598 --> 00:08:56.165
I wasn't sure
how many books to bring.

00:08:56.208 --> 00:08:58.080
Do not trouble yourself
with the journey.

00:08:58.123 --> 00:09:01.257
The Farm cures all.

00:09:10.614 --> 00:09:12.616
So, we were surrounded
by four Borg, right?

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.662
And nobody ever talks
about this, but they smell

00:09:14.705 --> 00:09:15.880
like old trash bags.

00:09:15.924 --> 00:09:18.013
What? Four?How'd you get out?

00:09:18.056 --> 00:09:20.276
It required unorthodox tactics.

00:09:20.319 --> 00:09:23.409
Durga kicked their buttswith Vulcan jujitsu.

00:09:23.453 --> 00:09:25.063
Yeah, well,
this one time, Ramsey and I

00:09:25.107 --> 00:09:27.457
stole Professor Rubichik's
old, special car

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.719
and drove it into the bay.

00:09:28.763 --> 00:09:30.634
It was hilarious.
He was so pissed.

00:09:30.678 --> 00:09:33.506
I love Saul Rubichek.He was my mentor at the Academy.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.160
That car was his life.

00:09:35.204 --> 00:09:37.815
-I spoke at his funeral.
-Uh, well, that was
a long time ago.

00:09:37.859 --> 00:09:39.425
I still do stuff like that
all the time.

00:09:39.469 --> 00:09:42.515
Last week, I put a scorpion
in Ransom's bed.

00:09:42.559 --> 00:09:44.256
It was bad. He almost died.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.084
Do you often disrupt missions?

00:09:46.128 --> 00:09:48.652
: No, I mean, I do
regular Starfleet stuff, too.

00:09:48.696 --> 00:09:50.567
Everyone ready?

00:09:50.611 --> 00:09:52.700
Let's roll out.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.969
Reports indicate
that first contact here

00:10:01.012 --> 00:10:02.666
was a little tricky.
The bogs didn't help.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.668
Let's see if we can get ahold
of the local authorities.

00:10:04.712 --> 00:10:06.539
-Copy that.

00:10:07.628 --> 00:10:09.717
Hey, are you
on a different mission,

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:10.892
or are you coming with us?

00:10:10.935 --> 00:10:12.415
Oh. Uh, sorry. Right.

00:10:12.458 --> 00:10:14.373
I'll just, uh...

00:10:16.462 --> 00:10:18.726
When we're done here,
you'll be back to enjoying

00:10:18.769 --> 00:10:21.032
crystal clear water,
King Phibeas.

00:10:21.076 --> 00:10:24.079
We osmose
our most brackish gratitude.

00:10:26.298 --> 00:10:27.517
MARINER:
So, uh, you and Ramsey

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.649
are pretty tight, huh?
How'd you guys meet?

00:10:28.692 --> 00:10:30.520
I do not believe
that information

00:10:30.563 --> 00:10:32.522
has any bearing
on our current objective.

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:34.524
Damn, Durga.
I was just making chitchat.

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.308
-WARREN:
Critical overpressure.

00:10:36.352 --> 00:10:38.615
One of the cascade valves
must be jammed open!

00:10:38.659 --> 00:10:39.964
We've got 30 seconds

00:10:40.008 --> 00:10:41.357
till the whole system blows!

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.793
Mariner, the tricorders.

00:10:42.837 --> 00:10:44.708
Um, uh, I...
You know, I think I left them

00:10:44.752 --> 00:10:45.927
in the transporter room.

00:10:48.756 --> 00:10:50.714
Try clearing it
with a subsonic pulse.

00:10:55.414 --> 00:10:57.329
MARINER:
I must have grabbed
the wrong crate.

00:10:57.373 --> 00:10:59.767
I-I left all our tricorders
back on the Cerritos.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:02.639
Which is the least useful placefor them to be,

00:11:02.683 --> 00:11:05.424
First Officer Mariner.

00:11:05.468 --> 00:11:07.688
FREEMAN:
Captain Ramsey,

00:11:07.731 --> 00:11:09.646
I just wanted to take
a brief pause

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.823
from our covert operation
to check in

00:11:12.867 --> 00:11:14.825
-on my ship.
-The Cerritosand her crew

00:11:14.869 --> 00:11:17.001
have performed admirably,
Captain Freeman.

00:11:17.045 --> 00:11:18.742
We've repaired the waste pipe
on Khwopa

00:11:18.786 --> 00:11:19.874
and are waiting on the Rubidoux.

00:11:19.917 --> 00:11:21.789
Very good. I've got to go.

00:11:21.832 --> 00:11:24.400
These rulot seeds
are highly volatile.

00:11:24.443 --> 00:11:27.490
I may be called to plant them
at any moment.

00:11:27.533 --> 00:11:29.231
Godspeed, Captain.

00:11:29.274 --> 00:11:32.103
Okay, so,
they mightplant seeds?

00:11:32.147 --> 00:11:35.019
Well, sounds like they're
on a very important mission.

00:11:35.063 --> 00:11:38.849
Strange. The Rubidoux
should have arrived by now.

00:11:38.893 --> 00:11:40.677
Well, Captain Dayton
isn't exactly punctual,

00:11:40.721 --> 00:11:43.375
but we may as well follow up.
Initiate long-range scan.

00:11:44.463 --> 00:11:46.117
Mariner,

00:11:46.161 --> 00:11:47.902
-if you don't mind?
-Oh! Me.

00:11:47.945 --> 00:11:49.425
Right.  Sure thing.

00:11:49.468 --> 00:11:50.905
-Uh, here we go.

00:11:50.948 --> 00:11:53.298
Ah! Uh, s-sorry! Hold on. Uh...

00:11:53.342 --> 00:11:55.692
Perhaps Mariner isn't as apt
as you recall.

00:11:55.736 --> 00:11:57.346
Nobody move! Just wait. It'll...

00:11:57.389 --> 00:11:59.174
-It'll tire itself out.
-: Hey.

00:11:59.217 --> 00:12:01.611
--Just breathe. You've got this.-Uh...

00:12:12.578 --> 00:12:13.710
Huh.

00:12:15.843 --> 00:12:16.887
Wow, I never knew there were

00:12:16.931 --> 00:12:18.454
this many accidents
in Starfleet.

00:12:18.497 --> 00:12:20.935
Which is exactly why
Division 14 exists:

00:12:20.978 --> 00:12:23.851
to hide the mistakesStarfleet would like to ignore.

00:12:23.894 --> 00:12:26.244
-Oh, well, that doesn't
sound very Starfleety.
-The admirals

00:12:26.288 --> 00:12:28.725
wouldn't want to jeopardizethe allegiance of their officers

00:12:28.769 --> 00:12:30.727
by forcing them
to work alongside

00:12:30.771 --> 00:12:32.773
a man whose body is equal parts

00:12:32.816 --> 00:12:34.992
accelerated growth
and reverse aging.

00:12:35.036 --> 00:12:38.126
That's right. Stare at me.

00:12:38.169 --> 00:12:39.736
-I-I wasn't s-staring.
-The freak

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.956
infected by an alien horse bite,

00:12:41.999 --> 00:12:45.220
doomed to live out his days
as half a rascal.

00:12:45.263 --> 00:12:48.614
Everyone would rather averttheir gaze instead of curing us.

00:12:48.658 --> 00:12:50.703
We're inconvenient.

00:12:50.747 --> 00:12:53.010
But aren't there specialists
who specialize in this?

00:12:53.054 --> 00:12:54.838
Tell that to Ensign Jenna,

00:12:54.882 --> 00:12:57.101
exposed to delta radiation.

00:12:57.145 --> 00:12:58.711
Or Ellis and Sanderson.

00:12:58.755 --> 00:13:01.671
Neutrino field
transporter accident.

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:04.456
-We have two of everything.
-Almost everything.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.894
And Anthony.

00:13:09.113 --> 00:13:11.681
Hi, Anthony.
Did it used to be a man?

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:13.552
Yeah,
that's what we're assuming.

00:13:13.596 --> 00:13:16.207
Don't worry, The Dog. You don'tbelong here with these freaks.

00:13:16.251 --> 00:13:17.600
I'll break you out
first chance I get.

00:13:17.643 --> 00:13:19.210
Come on, you're making it
sound worse than it is.

00:13:19.254 --> 00:13:21.430
I mean, we're all going
to a resort planet

00:13:21.473 --> 00:13:23.171
with gentle nurses and whatnot.

00:13:23.214 --> 00:13:24.825
-It's gonna be great.

00:13:24.868 --> 00:13:26.348
The Farm?

00:13:26.391 --> 00:13:29.917
You really think they'retaking us to a paradise planet?

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:32.049
Wait, yeah. I...
Then where are we going?

00:13:32.093 --> 00:13:35.096
Nowhere.
We've been here for months.

00:13:35.139 --> 00:13:37.402
-This isThe Farm!

00:13:47.369 --> 00:13:48.936
It's the Rubidoux,Captain.

00:13:48.979 --> 00:13:50.633
All systems
appear to be off-line.

00:13:50.676 --> 00:13:53.288
I told Dayton to get her energycoils replaced last month.

00:13:53.331 --> 00:13:54.898
Looks like I was right.

00:13:54.942 --> 00:13:57.379
If power's out, they're probablyholed up in a safe room,

00:13:57.422 --> 00:13:59.990
waiting for rescue,
just like last time.

00:14:00.034 --> 00:14:01.426
Durga, Mariner, Warren,

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.950
you're with me.
Let's give them a jump.

00:14:09.391 --> 00:14:11.915
Power has been interrupted
in engineering.

00:14:11.959 --> 00:14:13.699
Durga, get the main systems
back on line.

00:14:13.743 --> 00:14:15.876
Mariner and I will figure out
where the crew is holed up.

00:14:15.919 --> 00:14:17.660
Should be a simple repair
for me, Captain.

00:14:17.703 --> 00:14:19.836
Check in every 15 minutes.
Oh, and someone make sure

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.272
to get a picture of me
and Captain Dayton

00:14:21.316 --> 00:14:23.187
when she thanks me
for saving her ass again.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.327
Sorry. Uh, new boots.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:35.504
Wait is going on with you?I really need you to step it up.

00:14:35.547 --> 00:14:37.245
Sorry. Yeah, no, I'll do better.

00:14:37.288 --> 00:14:39.203
You know, it's these darn boots.
These boots are, like...

00:14:39.247 --> 00:14:40.726
I got... I...
Well, I wanted to get,

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.946
-like, a taller boot.
-Stop with the boots!

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.208
-What's up, girl?

00:14:44.252 --> 00:14:46.080
What's wrong? You...
You want walkies?

00:14:46.123 --> 00:14:48.125
Oh, come on. Let's go.

00:14:50.867 --> 00:14:54.392
Listen up.There's a shift change at 0200.

00:14:54.436 --> 00:14:56.742
It's our chance
to take the ship.

00:14:56.786 --> 00:14:58.005
You're talking about a mutiny.

00:14:58.048 --> 00:15:00.311
Exactly.
We'll find our own planet

00:15:00.355 --> 00:15:03.314
where we won't be treated like
failed science experiments.

00:15:03.358 --> 00:15:06.665
Tonight, freaks fight back!

00:15:06.709 --> 00:15:08.711
: Freaks fight back!
Freaks fight back!

00:15:08.754 --> 00:15:11.844
Brother, freaks united
are freaks no more.

00:15:11.888 --> 00:15:14.195
Say it with me.
Freaks fight back!

00:15:14.238 --> 00:15:16.675
Yeah. Freaks fight back.

00:15:16.719 --> 00:15:18.112
Freaks fight back!

00:15:18.155 --> 00:15:20.201
Freaks fight back!
Freaks fight back!

00:15:20.244 --> 00:15:22.420
...is what they were all
chanting. We were all doing it

00:15:22.464 --> 00:15:24.422
in unison.

00:15:24.466 --> 00:15:27.164
Mutiny? On my ship?
How dare they!

00:15:27.208 --> 00:15:28.774
Sir, they just want
more information.

00:15:28.818 --> 00:15:30.733
I think if we all sat down
in a conference room

00:15:30.776 --> 00:15:32.604
-and talked it out...

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.827
-If those freaks
think they can mutiny,

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.917
they're in for a rude awakening.

00:15:40.961 --> 00:15:43.354
No, no, no! The only reason Itold you is so nobody gets hurt.

00:15:43.398 --> 00:15:45.530
We're all Starfleet.
We have to follow the rules.

00:15:45.574 --> 00:15:47.445
-I amthe rules.
-Wait!

00:15:47.489 --> 00:15:49.099
We can talk this out! Sir!
Don't tell them I tattled!

00:15:49.143 --> 00:15:50.144
Don't tell them I tattled!

00:15:50.187 --> 00:15:51.884
MARINER:
Um, hello?

00:15:51.928 --> 00:15:54.626
Hello, Rubidouxpeople? Hello?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.106
Oh, where are these guys?

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:58.239
How do you do this every day?
It is so boring.

00:15:58.282 --> 00:15:59.631
You used to love
space mysteries.

00:15:59.675 --> 00:16:00.850
Yeah. I used to be dumb.

00:16:00.893 --> 00:16:02.373
That's one way to look at it.

00:16:02.417 --> 00:16:04.245
-What does that mean?
-I expected

00:16:04.288 --> 00:16:05.986
to be working with
the capable Starfleet badass

00:16:06.029 --> 00:16:08.379
I knew at the Academy,
not whatever you are now.

00:16:08.423 --> 00:16:10.729
Yeah, and I expected to be
working with my fun friend,

00:16:10.773 --> 00:16:11.904
-not a total...
-Hold it.

00:16:11.948 --> 00:16:13.863
These doors
have been manually sealed.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.702
- I don't want to die.
-Stand down. We're Starfleet.

00:16:26.745 --> 00:16:28.356
-I don't want to die.
I don't want to die.
-Captain Dayton.

00:16:28.399 --> 00:16:29.922
Whoa, Captain, Captain,
you're gonna be okay.

00:16:29.966 --> 00:16:31.707
No! That thing is still
out there!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.883
There's nothing outside
except the Cerritos.

00:16:33.926 --> 00:16:36.712
You don't understand!
We're inside of it!

00:16:36.755 --> 00:16:40.237
It's time.
Let's shake the ship!

00:16:40.281 --> 00:16:42.370
-What do you think you're doing?-Uh... nothing.

00:16:42.413 --> 00:16:43.719
Mutiny makes you traitors!

00:16:43.762 --> 00:16:46.939
Mutiny?
No, these are just props

00:16:46.983 --> 00:16:49.507
that we're using for our...
our musical, right, guys?

00:16:49.551 --> 00:16:52.902
Stop lying! Boimler told me
everything! Brad Boimler.

00:16:52.945 --> 00:16:54.077
-Ooh, no, no, no.
-Right there-- Brad Boimler.

00:16:54.121 --> 00:16:55.905
Boimler, what the hell?!

00:16:55.948 --> 00:16:57.863
Freaks fight back?

00:16:57.907 --> 00:17:00.779
From now on, everyone is
confined to their quarters.

00:17:00.823 --> 00:17:02.912
I suggest
you spend the time alone,

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:05.654
thinking about how
to be more like Brad.

00:17:05.697 --> 00:17:08.744
Wait, wait, wait. I have no ideahow he found out, guys.

00:17:08.787 --> 00:17:10.746
-That's crazy.
-Get the rat!

00:17:10.789 --> 00:17:12.791
-Get him!
-Guys, no. Help!
So many freaks!

00:17:12.835 --> 00:17:15.620
We shut down systemsbecause it feeds on electricity.

00:17:15.664 --> 00:17:17.927
Durga, do not restore power.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.798
RAMSEY: Durga, Durga...
restore power.

00:17:19.842 --> 00:17:21.844
Captain, artificial gravity
is coming back on line.

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:29.895
-What the hell?!

00:17:29.939 --> 00:17:31.854
Oh, stop it!
Stop it! Stop it!

00:17:31.897 --> 00:17:33.986
How big is this thing?

00:17:41.211 --> 00:17:43.431
All right, everyone with me.
We need to stay calm.

00:17:45.433 --> 00:17:46.956
Hallway, now!

00:17:46.999 --> 00:17:49.828
Ramsey to Cerritos.Prepare for emergency transport.

00:17:49.872 --> 00:17:53.093
Damn thing must be
blocking signals.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:56.879
I don't want to die in space!
I don't want to die in space!

00:17:56.922 --> 00:17:59.273
-We're all gonna...
-Pick her up.

00:17:59.316 --> 00:18:01.144
We have to get to the bridge.
That's where we beamed in.

00:18:01.188 --> 00:18:03.146
-There's a good chance
we can still get a signal out.
-Ugh.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:05.148
Where has thisMariner been
all day?

00:18:05.192 --> 00:18:06.323
-I don't know what
you're talking about.
-No, no, no, no.

00:18:06.367 --> 00:18:08.151
Something's going on here.

00:18:08.195 --> 00:18:10.066
Been non-stop screwing up,
then suddenly, you're back

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.415
to taking charge and
punching out captains and...

00:18:11.459 --> 00:18:12.416
Wait a minute.

00:18:14.462 --> 00:18:16.464
Maybe let's talk, like, after
the giant space emergency.

00:18:16.507 --> 00:18:18.422
You were taking a dive,
weren't you?

00:18:18.466 --> 00:18:20.294
You figured out I was gonnaoffer you a spot on the
Oakland.

00:18:20.337 --> 00:18:22.731
Yeah, well, maybe
I didn't want my best friend

00:18:22.774 --> 00:18:24.298
trying to trick me
into a job I didn't want.

00:18:24.341 --> 00:18:26.300
-You ever think of that?
-Ugh!

00:18:26.343 --> 00:18:27.736
We all thought you'd be the
first captain from our class.

00:18:27.779 --> 00:18:30.391
You got the best grades,
you kept us all on track.

00:18:30.434 --> 00:18:32.610
Now it seems like
you don't even like Starfleet.

00:18:32.654 --> 00:18:35.265
You used to do whateveryou wanted whenever you wanted.

00:18:35.309 --> 00:18:37.572
Now you got to check in
with Durga every five minutes.

00:18:37.615 --> 00:18:40.879
Because I love leading a team
that puts their trust in me.

00:18:40.923 --> 00:18:42.403
Fine, but I don't love

00:18:42.446 --> 00:18:43.621
that everyone's
always screaming at me

00:18:43.665 --> 00:18:44.883
to rank up and take charge.

00:18:44.927 --> 00:18:46.885
Why can't I just be
a super great ensign?

00:18:46.929 --> 00:18:48.931
Look, how about you stop
pretending to be a ,

00:18:48.974 --> 00:18:50.585
and I'll stop trying
to recruit you,

00:18:50.628 --> 00:18:53.457
-and we can go save
these people?
-Deal!

00:18:55.067 --> 00:18:56.025
-Got you.

00:18:56.068 --> 00:18:58.680
A rat trapped in an airlock.

00:18:58.723 --> 00:19:00.508
That sounds about right.

00:19:00.551 --> 00:19:02.162
Any last words?

00:19:02.205 --> 00:19:03.424
Please don't hurt me.
Please don't hurt me!

00:19:03.467 --> 00:19:05.426
I'm just a freak like you, see?

00:19:07.167 --> 00:19:09.125
It wore off!
I'm not a freak anymore!

00:19:09.169 --> 00:19:11.519
Hey, would you look at that!
Great!

00:19:11.562 --> 00:19:13.564
You're normal now.

00:19:13.608 --> 00:19:15.523
Enjoy your walk in space.

00:19:20.484 --> 00:19:23.705
Wait. Why is the air not
being forced from my lungs?

00:19:25.228 --> 00:19:27.361
The Farm! It's real?

00:19:27.404 --> 00:19:29.319
Isn't it beautiful?
The missions might be long,

00:19:29.363 --> 00:19:32.453
but it's worth it
every time we get back.

00:19:32.496 --> 00:19:34.672
Ooh! Do I have egg on my face.

00:19:34.716 --> 00:19:36.631
Sir, I'm sorry for the whole...

00:19:36.674 --> 00:19:38.807
-mutiny thing.
-I get it.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.462
The Farm does seem unbelievable.

00:19:41.505 --> 00:19:44.029
No, I'm sorry I reacted
the way I did.

00:19:44.073 --> 00:19:45.335
We should have just
talked it out.

00:19:45.379 --> 00:19:47.250
Which is what I said
we should do!

00:19:47.294 --> 00:19:49.992
Next time, we'll avoid
a mutiny beforeit happens.

00:19:50.035 --> 00:19:52.429
Maybe paint the ship
some friendlier colors,

00:19:52.473 --> 00:19:54.736
turn on some lights
so it isn't so creepy.

00:19:54.779 --> 00:19:58.261
Enjoy your path
to recovery, my friends.

00:20:01.873 --> 00:20:03.397
Oh, it's just the way I laugh.

00:20:16.366 --> 00:20:18.281
This is where
we have to say goodbye.

00:20:18.325 --> 00:20:20.152
I never wanted to leave you.

00:20:20.196 --> 00:20:22.329
You're not a freak.
You're just a good dog.

00:20:22.372 --> 00:20:25.157
I will never give up trying
to get you back home.

00:20:25.201 --> 00:20:28.248
Tendi, you have been
an exemplary creator.

00:20:28.291 --> 00:20:30.728
But do not cry.
I like it here!

00:20:30.772 --> 00:20:32.426
There's far more space to run

00:20:32.469 --> 00:20:34.602
and many fascinating things
upon which to urinate.

00:20:34.645 --> 00:20:37.300
Oh, wow.
I'm so glad you're happy!

00:20:37.344 --> 00:20:40.042
Well, The Dog,
then I guess this is goodbye.

00:20:40.085 --> 00:20:41.565
Farewell, Tendi.

00:20:41.609 --> 00:20:45.395
May the suns shine upon you.

00:20:47.049 --> 00:20:48.703
Wait. You knew
she could talk and walk?

00:20:48.746 --> 00:20:50.574
Yeah, of course she can talk.
She's a dog.

00:20:50.618 --> 00:20:53.447
-Normal dogs don't do any
of that stuff.
-They don't?

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:55.623
Wait. But normal dogshover and spit lightning, right?

00:20:55.666 --> 00:20:58.495
-No, none of that!
-Oh!

00:20:58.539 --> 00:21:01.019
Well, then this is starting
to make a lot more sense.

00:21:01.063 --> 00:21:03.500
Hey, you area freak.

00:21:03.544 --> 00:21:06.416
I know!I just didn't want you to worry.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.679
Oh, she's such a good girl.

00:21:08.723 --> 00:21:12.030
Oh, we call dibs on this cutie.

00:21:12.074 --> 00:21:13.597
-: Oh.
-No, he shouldn't

00:21:13.641 --> 00:21:15.643
even be here.
He's not a freak anymore.

00:21:15.686 --> 00:21:17.819
-You're not?
-I, uh, I have acid reflux.

00:21:17.862 --> 00:21:20.256
That's kind of freakish.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.606
Wait, wait, wait!

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.304
No.

00:21:33.138 --> 00:21:35.663
Not today, snot!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:44.498
-Durga, report.

00:21:44.541 --> 00:21:47.849
There's some sort of alien
entity inside the ship.

00:21:47.892 --> 00:21:49.546
-Oh, you think?
-Okay, everybody,

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:50.591
we're gonna get you out of here.

00:21:54.203 --> 00:21:57.032
-Warren, beam us out of here.
-I'm trying. There's too many.

00:21:57.075 --> 00:22:00.601
-We-we won't have time.


-Rutherford!

00:22:00.644 --> 00:22:02.385
We need your transporter
thing up and running now!

00:22:02.429 --> 00:22:03.560
It made Boimler weird!

00:22:03.604 --> 00:22:04.692
Boim us out of here!

00:22:07.085 --> 00:22:10.437
-Hold on!
-Rutherford!

00:22:18.793 --> 00:22:20.708
Come on, baby.
Give Rutherford the juice!

00:22:31.675 --> 00:22:33.547
Oh, man, I knew
you could do it, Ruthy!

00:22:33.590 --> 00:22:35.418
Why are we still in phase?

00:22:35.462 --> 00:22:36.985
Ah, it's just cosmetic.

00:22:37.028 --> 00:22:41.642
-It's just cosmetic.

00:22:45.472 --> 00:22:47.474
RAMSEY:
Captain's log.

00:22:47.517 --> 00:22:49.954
The evacuation of the U.S.S.
Rubidoux was a success,

00:22:49.998 --> 00:22:52.566
thanks to the quick thinking
of theCerritos crew.

00:22:52.609 --> 00:22:55.873
While the exact classification of this space entity eludes us,

00:22:55.917 --> 00:23:00.051
we believe it to be peaceful,
in search of a home.

00:23:01.792 --> 00:23:03.011
You're cured?

00:23:03.054 --> 00:23:04.534
I mean, see?
I knew you'd be fine.

00:23:04.578 --> 00:23:06.580
Listen, you got
to mess me up again.

00:23:06.623 --> 00:23:08.538
Not permanently, but maybe,
like, a nice two-week freak.

00:23:08.582 --> 00:23:10.714
I have been tinkering
with some ancient plasmas.

00:23:10.758 --> 00:23:13.456
Aw. Good afternoon.
I'm Tendi.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.024
How are you today?
Ugh. Ugh!

00:23:16.067 --> 00:23:18.940
Ugh! She licked me.
What a weirdo!

00:23:18.983 --> 00:23:20.724
Would you look at that?

00:23:20.768 --> 00:23:22.683
Nothing like a big,
crazy alien to remind you

00:23:22.726 --> 00:23:24.946
why "space explorer" is
such a great gig.

00:23:24.989 --> 00:23:26.600
Yeah, it's the best.

00:23:26.643 --> 00:23:29.820
Well, Starfleet isn't perfect,
but my offer still stands.

00:23:29.864 --> 00:23:32.910
If you want a chance to leadby example, I'd have your back.

00:23:32.954 --> 00:23:36.174
Yeah, if I was gonna rank up
for anyone, it would be you,

00:23:36.218 --> 00:23:37.959
but, you know, I still have
some stuff to figure out

00:23:38.002 --> 00:23:39.874
while I'm lower decks,
about who Iwant to be.

00:23:39.917 --> 00:23:42.703
Like, maybe I'll buckle down
and become a captain.

00:23:42.746 --> 00:23:44.313
Maybe I won't.
Probably won't.

00:23:44.356 --> 00:23:46.402
-I just need time to find me.
-I know you will.

00:23:46.446 --> 00:23:49.536
Well, well, well,
beautiful Captain Ramsey.

00:23:49.579 --> 00:23:51.538
I'd love to buy you a drink.

00:23:52.756 --> 00:23:55.629
Oh. Sorry, Ransom.
Instincts kicked in.

00:23:55.672 --> 00:23:57.674
